    </content>
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001">
    <term>epiphyses</term>
    <meaning>ends of long bones like the ones in arms and legs</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00002">
    <term>future orientation</term>
    <meaning>ability to think about and plan for what lies ahead, including predicting the consequences of one’s actions</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00003">
    <term>obesity</term>
    <meaning>when an individual’s BMI is over 30; correlated with many health issues including high blood pressure, diabetes, and heart disease</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00004">
    <term>obesity paradox</term>
    <meaning>observation that people with a high BMI who develop heart disease sometimes live longer and are in better health than people with a lower BMI who develop heart disease</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00005">
    <term>presbyopia</term>
    <meaning>difficulty seeing things close up due to changes in the lens of the eye</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00006">
    <term>substance abuse</term>
    <meaning>use of drugs or alcohol in excess or for purposes for which they weren’t intended, leading to problems in physical, social, and/or psychological functioning, often termed substance misuse or problematic substance use in order to avoid stigma of "abuse"; often related to substance use disorder (SUD)</meaning>
    </definition>
    </glossary>
    </document>